-- title:
--   Restriction of a component ideal to a distinct component is invertible
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N₀$ and $p$ with $N₀$ nonzero and $p$ prime, a proof $hpN₀$ that $p \nmid N₀$, and a model package $𝔓 : \mathrm{DRModelPackageLevel}\ N₀\ p\ hpN₀$. Let $O$ be a commutative ring equipped with a ring homomorphism $ρO : \mathrm{DRLevel.R}\ p \to O$, let $κ$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $toκ : O \to κ$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $R$ be a resolved model package $\mathrm{DRResolvedModelPackageLevel}\ N₀\ p\ 𝔓\ O\ ρO\ κ\ toκ$; among its data are a scheme $R.Y$ proper and flat over $\operatorname{Spec} O$ and a family $R.\mathrm{comp}$ of ideal sheaf data on $R.Y$ indexed by $\mathrm{X0MqComponents}\ R.\mathrm{width} = \mathrm{Fin}\ 2 \oplus \Sigma_{n}\,\mathrm{Fin}(R.\mathrm{width}\ n - 1)$, each of them invertible, with integral associated closed subscheme, together with marked points $R.η\ v$ and the stalk condition $R.η\_\mathrm{stalk}$. Let $v$ and $w$ be two indices with $v \neq w$. Then the ideal sheaf data obtained by pulling back $R.\mathrm{comp}\ v$ along the closed immersion $(R.\mathrm{comp}\ w).\mathrm{subschemeι}$ of the subscheme cut out by $R.\mathrm{comp}\ w$ is invertible, i.e. every point $x$ of that subscheme admits an affine open $U$ and a section $f \in Γ(U)$ with $x$ in the basic open set $D(f)$, such that on the affine open $D(f)$ the pulled-back ideal is generated by a single non-zero-divisor.
--
--   This is the statement that, on a regular model of $X_0(N₀p)$, the scheme-theoretic restriction of one component of the special fibre to a distinct component is an effective Cartier divisor on the latter. It feeds the Euler-characteristic computations for the component sheaves of the resolved model package, where intersection numbers of distinct components are computed through invertible sheaves on each component.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRResolvedModelPackageLevel_isInvertible_comap_comp_subschemeIota.lean

